//! The concatenation window tables, from `LoqTTS6.so`.
//!
//! Generated by `tools/genwindow.py`; do not hand-edit. Both are
//! exported `OBJECT` symbols of 628 `i16`.
//!
//! `SigCoseno` is a **half-Hann falling from 1 to 0** and matches
//! `round(32767 * (1 + cos(pi*i/628)) / 2)` to within 1 -- which is why
//! it is transcribed rather than computed: an error of 1 in the window
//! is an error of 1 in the output, and the gate here is byte-exactness.
//!
//! `SigCosCubo` is steeper and has **no known closed form** (the
//! log-ratio test rules out any `cos^p` or `Hann^p` family). It reaches
//! zero at index 533, well before the end, so a fade using it finishes
//! early. Treat it as a literal table.

